

NUL                         Definition                        NUL




NNUULL is the ASCII null character ` '.  Do not  confuse it with the
null  pointer NULL  or with  the empty  string "".   A C-language
string is  always terminated with a NUL.  The  empty string "" is
an array of cchhaarrs with only one element, namely a NUL.

